{"title":"2012 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 17","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Similar_to_solution_1_but_more_detailed)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Similar to solution 1 but more detailed)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_FormulaFocus_(Logical,_Good_Editing,_~0:55)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by FormulaFocus (Logical, Good Editing, ~0:55)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> be a subset of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/4/6d42bcf7d3894918de0937c5e45ffd60bf143b31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{1,2,3,\\dots,30\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"119\" height=\"18\" /> with the property that no pair of distinct elements in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> has a sum divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.  What is the largest possible size of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/8/a084ddae99ed14e694154101d20f5abfa47c7630.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 10\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 13\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 15\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 16\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"397\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Of the integers from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/1/651ba418a810d971dbc8a326d49a71fe1541fae0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, there are six each of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/1/1b18aa2ff77bac5c3b67d1bcd138d42b41c3c577.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0,1,2,3,4\\ (\\text{mod}\\ 5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"142\" height=\"18\" />. We can create several rules to follow for the elements in subset <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />. No element can be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/2/962b9834100812cc962f6ece468a07b9a149c16b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\ (\\text{mod}\\ 5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"73\" height=\"18\" /> if there is an element that is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/1/4615ff7a3a0d232005e1833d08f881a5a6f7ed36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4\\ (\\text{mod}\\ 5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"73\" height=\"18\" />. No element can be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/9/b4950bea868f69976c75ab1cfd443388d8f8abc9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\ (\\text{mod}\\ 5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"73\" height=\"18\" /> if there is an element that is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/d/bdd06633089994fd07f608952c819106d0056c11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3\\ (\\text{mod}\\ 5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"73\" height=\"18\" />. Thus we can pick 6 elements from either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/2/962b9834100812cc962f6ece468a07b9a149c16b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\ (\\text{mod}\\ 5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"73\" height=\"18\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/1/4615ff7a3a0d232005e1833d08f881a5a6f7ed36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4\\ (\\text{mod}\\ 5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"73\" height=\"18\" /> and 6 elements from either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/9/b4950bea868f69976c75ab1cfd443388d8f8abc9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\ (\\text{mod}\\ 5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"73\" height=\"18\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/d/bdd06633089994fd07f608952c819106d0056c11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3\\ (\\text{mod}\\ 5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"73\" height=\"18\" /> for a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/a/dfa924fced204ed2cbf2c610b03466bc271ce89e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6+6=12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"82\" height=\"14\" /> elements. Considering <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/5/4453bbd886db776342c9948a1ce270602ee76594.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0\\ (\\text{mod}\\ 5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"73\" height=\"18\" />, there can be one element that is so because it will only be divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> if paired with another element that is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/5/4453bbd886db776342c9948a1ce270602ee76594.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0\\ (\\text{mod}\\ 5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"73\" height=\"18\" />. The final answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/790f18fe4ac4bc9d1db9917a645feff23ea2172e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\ 13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"64\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Similar_to_solution_1_but_more_detailed.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Similar_to_solution_1_but_more_detailed)\">Solution 2 (Similar to solution 1 but more detailed)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Similar to solution 1 but more detailed)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>[Errors to correct below: We don't totally discard <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/c/d2cd8ee8b389bd979238e1a49294cba9f143a60a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\pmod{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"83\" height=\"20\" />, since we can still have one of those. The <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> values are largest values, not quantities. So there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> numbers in each category.  We take <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> complete categories plus one from the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> category for a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.]\n</p><p>Since we are taking the sum of distinct numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/3/463e9e805999491680f948e17fc2723550b4067a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pmod{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"18\" />, the only values that can be the remainder is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. There are five different cases for the \"allowed\" modulos in the sequence, or the remainders that the sum of distinct elements are allowed to be in the sequence. They are:\n</p><p>1)      <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/0/180fb35c239b32a107e95b748e93bc5386bb6127.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0\\pmod{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"83\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><br />\n2)      <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/1/18101a87456bba84bf7101d3c4af5e6056ac204f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\pmod{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"83\" height=\"20\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/c/adc414005016eef22a076064e7c769f657d6d4ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3\\pmod{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"83\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><br />\n3)      <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/1/18101a87456bba84bf7101d3c4af5e6056ac204f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\pmod{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"83\" height=\"20\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/d/42d48d93b4088a9f6002e9d1e8c284d208d8c317.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\pmod{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"83\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><br />\n4)      <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/d/42d48d93b4088a9f6002e9d1e8c284d208d8c317.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\pmod{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"83\" height=\"20\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/5/605f8fd26e6ade92628c2eab22b1bd15ed60c8ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4\\pmod{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"83\" height=\"20\" />, \n</p><p><br />\n5)      <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/d/42d48d93b4088a9f6002e9d1e8c284d208d8c317.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\pmod{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"83\" height=\"20\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/1/18101a87456bba84bf7101d3c4af5e6056ac204f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\pmod{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"83\" height=\"20\" /> \n</p><p>Now, we can calculate the number of elements in each of these cases. For the first case, we rewrite <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/1/18101a87456bba84bf7101d3c4af5e6056ac204f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\pmod{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"83\" height=\"20\" /> in the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/d/b8dbfce8b1d8a84e90ccdfa22bd366615595cc8e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5k+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"16\" />. Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/a/feaa203bfd80ea1e19f31d169e3ab102bba289ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5k+1 &lt; 30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"95\" height=\"16\" />, which is the largest element in the sequence possible, we obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce5bb215d21ddfbe2ec17a99cb7118ca80e4a2ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=5$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />. In addition, for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/c/adc414005016eef22a076064e7c769f657d6d4ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3\\pmod{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"83\" height=\"20\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/3/1b35ed368e2950cd8f0adeff580e359715ee4844.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3x+5&lt;30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"95\" height=\"15\" />, whence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/c/51c80ea5862b45877f08d698a0c893bd2806a2fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />. This gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/d/60ded95a0834d28a52065eb22f590ee425f7d70b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5+5=10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"85\" height=\"15\" /> solutions since no matter which two numbers you choose, no sum can never be a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. The only possible remainders for the sum are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/e/abe31acca0190770c21ca8108afcd3918e18dc20.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/3/193b9b8ef461adf0e723da43776cfb7386b5ebd1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"40\" height=\"14\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/d/c4d3801d1226d2f2d2d0d9e8449e0269cac06927.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3+3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"40\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>In a similar manner, we calculate the element using the same logic. We find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/d/42d48d93b4088a9f6002e9d1e8c284d208d8c317.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\pmod{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"83\" height=\"20\" /> has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> elements, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/1/18101a87456bba84bf7101d3c4af5e6056ac204f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\pmod{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"83\" height=\"20\" /> has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> elements, meaning that there are a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> elements, which is the answer. \n~CharmaineMa07292010\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_FormulaFocus_.28Logical.2C_Good_Editing.2C_.7E0:55.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_FormulaFocus_(Logical,_Good_Editing,_~0:55)\">Video Solution by FormulaFocus (Logical, Good Editing, ~0:55)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by FormulaFocus (Logical, Good Editing, ~0:55)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/2dMdXV9BsYo\">https://www.youtube.com/shorts/2dMdXV9BsYo</a>\n</p><p>~Ebai\n</p><p>Note: the problem where this is linked is covered 0:20-1:15\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by OmegaLearn\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/orrw4VydBTk?t=483\">https://youtu.be/orrw4VydBTk?t=483</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12A\" title=\"2012 AMC 12A\">2012 AMC 12A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2012 AMC 12A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2012 AMC 12A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2012 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 16\">Problem 16</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2012 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 18\">Problem 18</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_1\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2012 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_2\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2012 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12A_